{"skill":{"slug":"google-meet-meetings","displayName":"Google Meet"},"version":{"version":"1.0.6","createdAt":1780989018740,"changelog":"Add UTM attribution tags (utm_source=clawhub) to ClawLink branding links so visits from this skill page are tracked as a distinct traffic source.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":14051,"sha256":"0d0b78b071c0f2d04651f7f07767ca5f6bb363f98b51f8dbac925f5b1916fda0","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2728,"sha256":"74859e8f60adc8e4eaa4281360a36639ee84d53e55e0ed9f14c05404481d7b14","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789545142777,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"44dccd124baebab8a2159cbaee5150cec5889de457a398e82fb7e5606cb554e7","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/44dccd124baebab8a2159cbaee5150cec5889de457a398e82fb7e5606cb554e7","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780992716820},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":0,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":0,"checkedAt":1789545142777},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This appears to be a legitimate Google Meet integration, but installing it means trusting a third-party ClawLink plugin with access to Meet data.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Hosted OAuth, token storage, and proxying Meet API requests are expected for this integration, but meeting transcripts, recordings, and participant records are sensitive and depend on ClawLink's handling and Google account permissions.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill tells the agent to install clawhub:clawlink-plugin, allowlist it, and restart the gateway after user confirmation; this is disclosed and purpose-aligned, but the package is not pinned to an immutable reviewed version.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The runtime instructions are scoped to Google Meet workflows, direct the agent to discover live Google Meet tools before use, and require confirmation and preview before write actions or ending an active conference.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The allowlist configuration and gateway restart make the plugin available across future OpenClaw chats, but the artifact does not install hidden services, scheduled tasks, backdoors, or unrelated persistence.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is Google Meet management through ClawLink, and the documented capabilities fit that purpose: creating spaces, reading conference records, participants, recordings, and transcripts, and ending active conferences.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install only if you trust ClawLink and the ClawHub plugin source. During setup, review the Google OAuth consent screen, confirm any create/update/end-meeting action before it runs, and know how to revoke the Google connection or remove the plugin if you no longer want it enabled.","findings":"[T08] expected: The artifact does instruct an unpinned ClawHub plugin install plus allowlisting and restart. That creates supply-chain trust in the ClawLink package, but the behavior is disclosed, requires user confirmation, and is coherent with making the integration work.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789545142777}}}}}